{#
  module/Application/view/application/index/sign-in-no-cookies.phtml — why signing in needs
  cookies.

  **Rendered by no route.** It is what `/user/login` and `/user/verify` answer with when the
  visitor has not consented, through App\JUser\CookieExplainer — at the requested URL, with a
  200, rather than by redirecting, which is what `Application\View\GdprStrategy::onRoute()`
  achieved by swapping the route match. A redirect would rewrite the address bar of someone
  who had just clicked an emailed link, and the point is that the link is still good once
  they consent: the token is spent only on a successful redemption.

  It sits under templates/content/ next to the pages ContentPageController serves, because
  that is where an Application-module static page belongs — but it has no route and will not
  get one. `/sign-in-no-cookies` was deleted from both front controllers on 2026-08-21: it
  had no guard entry, so default deny made it unreachable from the day it was written, and
  the only thing that ever showed the page was the route-match swap, which runs *after* the
  guard has approved a different route and needs no route of its own.

  Two faithful oddities, reproduced rather than fixed, because this port's evidence that
  nothing else moved is a byte-for-byte diff:

  - **the `<h1>` is "Sign In" and the sign-in page's is "Sign in".** Two separate phrases in
    the table, and that difference is how test/Smoke/UserSmokeTest tells which of the two
    pages it is looking at.
  - **the paragraph is not translated.** The .phtml prints it as a raw English literal with
    no `translate()` around it, so a German visitor who has refused cookies reads English.
    Filed in docs/BACKLOG.md rather than folded in — fixing it would put a new phrase in the
    table in the same change that moves the route.

  The .phtml sets no `headTitle()`, so the page title is passed **empty**. Absent would be a
  fatal: the layout reads `page_title` with no `is defined` guard under strict_variables, and
  the fatal arrives as a 200 with an empty body.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Sign In') }}</h1>

<p class="text-danger">Warning, without consenting to using cookies on this website, there is no way to sign in. Please accept consent, and <strong>reload the page</strong>.</p>
{% endblock %}
